        "node_id": "n_5_a64f04",
        "thought_text": "Thought-2: Instead of simulating every day up to \\(10^8\\) days, which is computationally expensive, we should simulate only the days when fogs actually appear. This reduces the number of iterations significantly and ensures that we accurately count the missed fogs without unnecessary computations. Additionally, we can use a set to keep track of the positions of the nets, allowing for efficient checks to see if a fog falls within the coverage of existing nets.",
